===Etymology===
{{etymon|en|id=country in southern Europe|inh|ang>Italia>Italy|tree=1|text=1}} Usually explained as a cognate of {{m|la|vitulus|t=calf}}, thus meaning "land of young bulls" in Oscan. In that case, ultimately from {{der|en|ine-pro|*wet-||year}}. According to some ancient Greek authors, named after a king ''Italus'' or ''Italos'', whose kingdom was on the peninsula.

